# data/opops/iprange.tsv — which core function owns an address.
#
# Copy to iprange.tsv and replace the examples with your own prefixes.
# Read by:  modules/11_lte_core.sh --gtp-screen-peer <ip> [message-type]
#           tools/lib/refdata.sh  refdata_opops_iprange <ip>
#
# Longest-prefix is NOT resolved: the first matching row wins, so put the
# narrow, specific prefixes above the broad ones.
#
# role: grx-peer | ipx-stp | core | smsc | hss | mme | pgw | sgw | dra | other
plmn	cidr	role	note
310-260	198.51.100.0/26	grx-peer	example: contracted roaming partner
310-260	203.0.113.0/28	ipx-stp	example: DX exchange signalling peer
310-260	10.0.0.0/8	core	example: the operator's own core
